# Build outputs from verification and hand-off builds. Only `dist/` was ignored, so every
# dist-<name>/ a verify tier or an agent produced was untracked-but-addable - and the round
# commit uses `git add -A`. Two of them (518 MB) were one commit away from the history on
# 2026-08-25. This does NOT untrack the ~22.6k dist files already in the index; that is a
# separate, deliberate cleanup.
dist-*/
.gauntlet-tmp/

# Transient publish worktree created by scripts/orchestration/publish_pass80.py.
# It was committed as a stray gitlink by a round `git add -A`; it is not a submodule.
.gh-pages-publish/

# Full duplicate repo checkouts left by a viewpoint-regression run and a bisect. Nothing
# references either; they were committed by a round `git add -A`. Tracking them made every
# repo-wide search return three copies of every source file.
.vp-regression-src/
.bisect-yesterday/

# Agent scratch: critic frame captures, a GLB before/after comparison, and a backup copy
# of three farcrysis sources whose originals live in src/. Committed by a round `git add -A`.
.critic-iw/
.tower-cmp-tmp/
.tmp-tree-mat-backup/

# Agent wave briefs handed to this worktree by the orchestrator. Repo content they
# are not: they are task instructions for an agent, and a round `git add -A` in an
# earlier attempt tracked them onto the shared branch.
local-claude-task-*.md

# Scratch checkouts the eye-clearance contract test writes into the repo root on
# purpose (scripts/qa/eye-clearance-sweep-contract.test.mjs: ES resolution walks
# up from the probe FILE, so a probe in os.tmpdir() cannot see node_modules and
# the bare `three` specifier the arena builders import fails). The test removes
# them in a finally block, but a killed or timed-out run leaves one behind - and
# on this machine other agents commit under you with `git add -A`.
.eye-clearance-probe-*/
